> integrate x^2 from 0 to 1
∫ x^2 dx
  = x^3/3 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 1] (max difference 1.1e-16)
  from 0 to 1: F(1) - F(0) = 0.333333333333333
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.333333333333333, estimated error 3.7e-15
  the two agree to 0
> integrate 2*x + 1 from 0 to 3
∫ 2x + 1 dx
  = x + 2x^2/2 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3] (max difference 0)
  from 0 to 3: F(3) - F(0) = 12
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 12, estimated error 0
  the two agree to 0
> integrate sin(x) from 0 to pi
∫ sin(x) dx
  = -cos(x) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3.14159] (max difference 0)
  from 0 to 3.14159: F(3.14159) - F(0) = 2
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 2, estimated error 2.2e-14
  the two agree to 0
