> integrate x^3 - 2x from -1 to 2
∫ x^3 - 2x dx
  = -2*x^2/2 + x^4/4 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-1, 2] (max difference 0)
  from -1 to 2: F(2) - F(-1) = 0.75
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.75, estimated error 8.3e-15
  the two agree to 2.2e-16
